      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "to determine whether functions of endothelial progenitor cells (EPCs) were impaired in patients with permanent atrial fibrillation (AF)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "35 patients with permanent AF (AF group) and 35 age and sex matched controls (control group) were collected. The numbers of circulating CD34+/KDR+ cells were determined with flow cytometry in the two groups. Cell proliferation, tube formation, nitric oxygen (NO) and vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) were assayed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "the numbers of CD34+/KDR+ cells were lower in the AF group than the control group (20.01 ± 12.66 /105 vs 77.93 ± 58.93 /105，p = 0.022). Colony formation unit (CFU) of EPCs were decreased in AF group compared to the control group（1.76 ± 0.59 CFU vs 3.45 ± 0.82 CFU, p = 0.0000). The AF group had lower cell proliferation ability than control group（0.401 ± 0.113 A vs 0.558 ± 0.130 A, p = 0.004). Tube formation ability was decreased in AF patients compared to controls（434.30 ± 96.22μm/mm2 vs 568.09 ± 196.17μm/mm2，p = 0.041). AF patients had lower VEGF secretion than controls (27.35 ± 9.93 ng/L vs 41.86 ± 7.31 ng/L，p = 0.001），they also had lower NO secretion than controls（16.55 ± 6.92μmol/l vs 23.65 ± 5.48，p = 0.012)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "proliferation, tube formation and paracrine of EPCs were reduced in patients with permanent AF."
        }
      ]},
